## Problem 3 — a timeout that escalates

Edit `ex3/solution.ts`. Implement:

```ts
export interface TimedResult {
  code: number | null;
  signal: NodeJS.Signals | null;
  stdout: string;
  timedOut: boolean;
  escalated: boolean;
}

export function runWithTimeout(
  file: string,
  args: readonly string[],
  options: { timeoutMs: number; graceMs?: number },
): Promise<TimedResult>
```

At `timeoutMs`, send `SIGTERM`. If the child has still not closed `graceMs`
later (default 100), send `SIGKILL` and set `escalated: true`. `timedOut` is
true whenever the deadline was reached, whether or not the escalation was
needed. A child that finishes on its own clears both timers.

```ts
await runWithTimeout(process.execPath, ["-e", "setTimeout(()=>{}, 60000)"], {
  timeoutMs: 50,
});
// { code: null, signal: "SIGTERM", timedOut: true, escalated: false, ... }
```

```
uv run dojo test node v3nc02_child_processes ex3
```

